<title>SWEDEN: Volvo May Europe new car registrations up 11.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Volvo May Europe new car registrations up 11.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish vehicle maker AB Volvo's new car registrations in western Europe rose 11.3 percent in May to 19,152 vehicles, the European Automobile Manufacturers' Association (ACEA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Saab Automobile AB's new car registrations fell 2.4 percent to 5,332, the group said.</p>
<p>The figures include the 15 members of the European Union, Switzerland, Norway and Liechtenstein.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
